        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "33a963c6-00a3-50a4-8177-4eaba263ae38",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Cliven Bundy, Ammon Bundy\n- Organizations: United States Bureau of Land Management\n- Events: 2014 Bundy standoff, occupation of the Malheur National Wildlife Refuge\n- Places: southeastern Nevada, Oregon\n- Concepts: grazing fees, federally owned land, legal disputes\n\nFacts:\n- Cliven Bundy was involved in a 21-year legal dispute with the United States Bureau of Land Management over grazing fees for his use of federally owned land adjacent to his ranch in southeastern Nevada.\n- The United States Bureau of Land Management obtained court orders directing Cliven Bundy to pay more than $1 million in withheld grazing fees.\n- The 2014 Bundy standoff was an armed confrontation between supporters of Cliven Bundy and law enforcement.\n- Ammon Bundy is the son of Cliven Bundy.\n- In 2016, Ammon Bundy led another armed standoff against the government during the occupation of the Malheur National Wildlife Refuge in Oregon.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
